    "body": "Part of #204. Binding acceptance: https://github.com/nicolas-found42/chief-of-staff-demo/issues/204\n\nCreate the shared projections that let dossier sections describe one consistent underlying record of work and relationships.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Expertise uses canonical subject categories with original source wording; claimed-only support and demonstrated work remain separately searchable and visible. No invented numeric expertise score.\n- Typed dated Person Connections distinguish direct collaboration, reporting, co-founding, co-authoring, funding/governance, and shared employer with no shared work. Direction and effective dates are preserved where meaningful.\n- Repeated collaboration derives from distinct shared Work Records with dates; mirrors/versions do not inflate counts and connections do not imply introductions or access.\n- Career/focus transitions and arguments/influences link to dated records. Similar vocabulary is not evidence of intellectual influence.\n- Activity views count observed dated artifacts by kind, with deduplication and coverage limits. They do not present commit/publication counts as total productivity or quality.\n- Compute capability intersections over active Workspace Profiles with demonstrated/claimed counts and completeness denominators. Unknown research cannot establish uniqueness.\n- Archive/merge/detach/source deletion invalidate these projections without losing independent support or historical source references.\n\nVerification: multi-person/shared-work fixtures; repeated collaboration across employers; separate same-employer-only edges; taxonomy aliases and claimed-to-demonstrated transitions; activity deduplication, sparse coverage, intersection denominators, and lifecycle invalidation.\n",
