    "body": "Part of #204. Binding acceptance: https://github.com/nicolas-found42/chief-of-staff-demo/issues/204\n\nReplace the primary maintenance-form experience with the dossier specified in #204. Use real persisted data; the earlier interactive mockup is design reference only.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Overview, career, body of work, expertise, writing/ideas, people/organisations, recognition, current context, and sources expose sourced summaries plus detailed records. The twenty coverage questions are not rendered as a questionnaire.\n- Source inspection opens retained text at supporting passages with original and retrieval dates, provenance, completeness, and independence context. Sections show gaps, staleness, conflict, and single-source support.\n- Progressive states distinguish queued/researching/incomplete/paused/source unavailable/no evidence/current within scope. Refresh in place without duplicate research or losing user navigation.\n- Relationship history is its own tab, referencing canonical Meetings, Transcript decisions/passages, Action Items, and Tasks. Public-only Profiles have a useful empty tab; private history is not copied into public sections.\n- Editing, merge/detach, revisions, archive/restore, and privacy deletion remain available as secondary maintenance. Select duplicate people by search/name, not raw internal IDs.\n- Provide accessible queue pause/resume/priority and budget controls, including backfill progress. New-person flow makes automatic research clear and does not require per-field acceptance.\n- Responsive keyboard-accessible reading and source inspection; deep links and exact historical Profile views continue to work.\n\nVerification: DOM/component tests for sparse/full/contested/private-only data and progressive states; Playwright journeys from each creation path into populated sources; accessibility/mobile checks and production bundle/container proof.\n",
